// cheap anti-entropy protocol. A node periodically asks one rotating peer for
// a digest (count/xor/sum) of its value set; the reply carries the peer's own
// digest. While traffic is flowing, digests almost always differ transiently
// (values are in flight), so full sets are only exchanged when both sides have
// been idle for a moment - which is exactly when a real divergence needs
// repairing. When idle, the protocol speeds up and walks through all peers, so
// any divergence heals well inside the recovery window before the final reads.
